  "film_direction": "**Palette:** 60% canvas (cream paper-anchor reads through mesh veil) / 30% hairline dashed rules + repeated canvas (no surface token; soft-editorial layers with translucency, not a second fill) / 10% accent — brand-primary (warm gold) carries hero words, CTA pill, and stat emphasis; brand-secondary (deep navy) reserved for ink and the brand-reveal scene's display type. Two-color limit per scene per preset rules. Ink stays brand-secondary navy throughout.\n**Type:** display (serif) = hero claims and scene anchors only; body (sans) = supporting copy, location labels, list items; mono = eyebrow metadata and chapter marks. Italic `<em>` is the system's only emphasis — no uppercase anywhere (soft-editorial voice register). Sentence case throughout.\n**Motion:** entries `EASE.entry`; heroes heavy; idle `EASE.drift`; exits none — scenes hold the final frame. Budget: one root-level camera move per scene (slow drift or dolly) + at most one breathing hero element; everything else rests. Stagger totals capped at 500ms.\n**Ambient:** brand-color mesh background (heavy veil, brand-primary gold + brand-secondary navy + brand-accent as three subtle atmospheric blobs, reading as a warm restrained base at viewing distance) — consistent across all scenes including closer. Sparse float particles in brand-primary at low opacity as the only coexisting layer.\n**Never (film-wide):** no drop shadows, no glow halos, no blur halos, no neon, no bokeh, no mesh gradients beyond the declared mesh default, no purple-blue AI gradient, no cards stacked on cards, no uppercase text, no dark ground scenes.\n**Transitions:** `crossfade` + `push-slide` as primary vocabulary; `zoom-through` reserved for the finale only.\n**Stillness-before-climax:** scenes 8 and 11 only.\n**Assets:** no `assetCandidates` provided in any scene — this is a text-driven film. Every scene relies on typographic composition, brand color, and component structures for visual density.",
